A||||16||Wannabe||Fiero Bashing||||1||
Z||000000||Wannabe||08-20-2001||04:00 PM||||Well, there is no longer any doubt. The thing I hate most about having a Fiero is the endless string of misinformation and "bad press" on the Fiero. Every time I tell people that I bought a Fiero to race with, they immediately have a huge selection of anecdotes to choose from like, "What, one of those fire traps?" or "That must be really hard work to keep it running" or "It must be a handful driving that thing with the Chevette suspension" (I have a Formula) blah blah blah. Best of all...."Why didn't you get a Honda?" The most polite description of  my choice of cars was "eclectic"<P>The strangest thing, I've owned two of these cars now, an '87 GT and my current '88 formula, and both have completly exceeded my expectations for reliability, low cost of repairs and maintenace and overall driving enjoyment.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Wannabe (edited 08-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fformula88||08-20-2001||05:05 PM||||It does get a little discourahging from time to time when people always ask about your "fire trap".  Unfortunately, the Fieros that did burn up sadled the car with a bad reputation for reliability, and its not going to go away.  <P>I do get an equal share of compliments on my Formula.  The 18 year old instant oil change techs are always in awe with the engine in the back.  It also gets a TON of looks from other drivers and pedestrians.  Its also the only car I have ever owned where you have people coming up to you all the time just to compliment the car, or say they used to own a Fiero and really liked it.<P>Next time they tell you to get a Honda, just shrug them off.  Those Honda guys have probably spent more $$ to make their cars fast and handle well than you paid for your whole car!  <P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||08-20-2001||06:34 PM||||When told of the Fiero as a fire trap, I tell them that, yeah, I know the problem, I have owned my 87 for about 15 years and it has only burned up three times, so that works out as a total rebuild every 5 years or so.  Some of them are smart enough to know I'm pulling their leg, but then there are those who....||||reg||1
Z||000003||Galen||08-20-2001||07:00 PM||||"three times? WOW, were you in it?"<P>hehe... <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/sig.gif">  Ray -    <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>    - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>www.FieroLinks.f2s.com</A><BR>AIM: GalenRPG - ICQ: 98668558||||reg||1
Z||000004||starfighter007@msn.com||08-20-2001||07:13 PM||||I say screw anybody that dont have anything nice to say.These type of people will always find something wrong with anything no matter what it is if its not theres.To bad there not around when you get ready to buy somthing so that they can pick it apart for you. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||kempo||08-20-2001||08:32 PM||||Tell them that a Honda is a riceburningpieceofdogcrap.  "A fiero... this is the car that makes life worth living!"  -2FastTom<P>-Kemp||||reg||1
Z||000006||formula2||08-20-2001||10:00 PM||||I know what you mean.. I have bought mine about 6 weeks ago.I post a topic on a local forum here in quebec.All I have read is negative response ..<P>So now you have a chevette ..<BR>My girlfriend had one and I still have nightmate ....<P><BR>I felt almoust sorry I bought that car..But this car is so much fun..Then I found this site and I told myself..Hey ,I am not the only  crazy guy on earth!!!!!!!!!!<BR>||||reg||12
Z||000007||Galen||08-21-2001||01:39 AM||||There a whole load of out of their mind ppl  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> some of us even have 2-3 of em..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> look at my 7..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Crazy crazy<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/sig.gif">  Ray -    <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>    - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>www.FieroLinks.f2s.com</A><BR>AIM: GalenRPG - ICQ: 98668558||||reg||1
Z||000008||artherd||08-21-2001||04:05 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fformula88:<BR><B><BR>I do get an equal share of compliments on my Formula.  The 18 year old instant oil change techs are always in awe with the engine in the back.  It also gets a TON of looks from other drivers and pedestrians.  Its also the only car I have ever owned where you have people coming up to you all the time just to compliment the car, or say they used to own a Fiero and really liked it.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>:) Totally!!  I think part of it is Trav's wheels, but my t-top gets rave reviews wherever it goes.  Even people who 'don't like' Fieros seem to like this one.  I went to visit a friend, and one of his buddies made some discouraging remarks, then he saw ther car... "Woah! Dude, no way **that's** a fiero!!!  Sweet car." <P>I met a gent the other day who used to work for GM and painted a score of cars over 20-odd years there.  One of them was the fiero.  I guarentee we'd have never met if I were driving a caviler or something not-fiero :)<BR>(I did congratulate him, my paint is <BR>stock, at 14 years old, it still looks basically new!<P>"Mid-engine, accept no substitutes!"<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000009||OcalaFiero||08-21-2001||08:46 AM||||We have a guy who races an '87 in our SCCA region (Central Florida). It was kind of neat to see him running at Daytona few weeks ago. Next race we have at Daytona, I'll drag the wife along to take some pics, as I'm usually a little busy flagging.||||reg||1
Z||000010||fierobaby||08-21-2001||11:25 AM||||I actually don't get bad comments on my car...well except once at a car show.. a guy was standing behind me and must have assumed since I was ayoung girl I did noit have a car entered in the show and he siad something along the lines of "Who would bring a Fiero here? ITs a nice color but a Fiero come on those cars are crap and always will be" I turned around and I was like "oh really?"<P>"yeah"<P>me: "do you knwo the owner of that car"<BR>him: "no"<BR>me: "well I'm pleased to meet you I own that 84 Pontiac Fiero in Candy Apply red not Med Mettalic Red like you said Sir. That car is far from crap" <P>and I walked awaty I think he was more stunned that I said somethign to him... :-) it was worth it!||||reg||1
Z||000011||rogergarrison||08-21-2001||01:02 PM||||I sorta get same thing even a car shows. When they find out its a kit, they act like its a volkswagen or something. Ferrari and Lambo kits dont get the same respect that the Cobras get.(Cobra kit) "Wow a Cobra !" (Ferrari kit)"oh thats just one of those fake kitcars." I just laugh them off knowing I can smoke most of them.||||reg||1
Z||000012||johnt671||08-21-2001||06:15 PM||||I get that a lot with my 84.  Then when I tell them that mine has almost 205,000 miles on it and is almost all original they are shocked that the car looks so good.  At this point I tell them that they all weren't bad.||||reg||1
Z||000013||pontiacs4me||08-21-2001||06:37 PM||||I dont try to tell anyone how good my car is after they bash it.  I just put up with it and take it like the truth, although I know its not.  I just know some day, with my stage 2 body kit, 17" tsw blades, turbocharged 3.4 liter and bright orange paint job, my car is not only going to look cooler than 99% of cars on the road, its also going to eat 99% of them for lunch, and that last 1% is going to have one hell of a run for their money.  Then all of those who called my fiero a piece of firetrap junk, can watch my taillights get smaller and smaller through their windshield.||||reg||1
Z||000014||artherd||08-21-2001||09:36 PM||||Yay!!<P>"Is that double stitch on polysynthetic rayon<BR>blend?"<BR>"er, Yes, of course" <BR>"You can't use double stitch on polysynthetic rayon, it rips the loops and the entire garment would fall apart. See you."<BR>- Rese Witherspoon in Legally Blonde.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierobaby:<BR><B>I actually don't get bad comments on my car...well except once at a car show.. a guy was standing behind me and must have assumed since I was ayoung girl I did noit have a car entered in the show and he siad something along the lines of "Who would bring a Fiero here? ITs a nice color but a Fiero come on those cars are crap and always will be" I turned around and I was like "oh really?"<P>"yeah"<P>me: "do you knwo the owner of that car"<BR>him: "no"<BR>me: "well I'm pleased to meet you I own that 84 Pontiac Fiero in Candy Apply red not Med Mettalic Red like you said Sir. That car is far from crap" <P>and I walked awaty I think he was more stunned that I said somethign to him... :-) it was worth it!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000015||Soelas||08-21-2001||10:16 PM||||I agree. right from day 1 when I bought my Fiero, I've heard nothing but insulting comments from ignorant people. When I first drove up in front of my friends place with my  1984 Fiero (that was in '95). Two of my more ignorant friends (who owned brand new dodge trucks) scoffed at me. Saying that i'd be nickled and dimed to death with repairs.<P>3 years later....when their warranties ran out.... it was amazing to see BOTH of them spending nearly $4000 canadian on some repairs to their vehicles (transmissions, transfer cases, suspension, etc) Just after I learned of their EXPENSIVE repairs (not to mention the price they paid for the trucks initially) I pointed out that my car had cost me $1600 CDN plus I had to replace the started and the oxygen sensor.....<P>When it all added up.... hmmmm...for the price they paid for one of their vehicles PLUS repairs.... I could've boughten at LEAST 15 of my Fieros.....<P>but let's remember what a piece of garbage a Fiero is...right?<P>People like this annoy me. I am currently working on my fiero and installing a v8 using one of Archie's kits. Besides the pats on the back I get from fellow Fiero owners...I've yet to receive a good comment from anyone else about it....other than "it's a waste of time".<P>Well.....I guess they've all exlluded themselves from riding in it when it's done  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Soelas <A HREF="http://www.soelas.ca" TARGET=_blank>www.soelas.ca</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000016||pontiacs4me||08-22-2001||01:55 AM||||I actually got a comment on my fiero today.  I was delivering pizzas for papa johns and when the customer answered the door he was looking at my car not me.  I said "how are you doing?"  he said "just fine, Wow those cars are classics"  I said "well not yet"  he said "you dont see them much anymore"  I said "you sure dont"  then he asked me if it had a turbo I said not yet, so he then asked if it was the four cylinder, I said no, and he looked kind of puzzled, so I told him it had the 2.8 liter v6, and he was like "oh, ok, thats cool"  and he said he liked it, and see ya later, thats about it.  Finally a complement to top off all the bashing.  Oh well.  My car has 178,000 miles on it, it hasnt caught fire yet, I dont think it will, unless someone dumps gas in it and throws in a match (knock on wood).  <BR>For the past 4 years Ive wanted a fiero.  I must of told my dad 200 times that I wanted a fiero, but he always told me how much of a piece of junk they were.  Get this, one day he tells me "When I used to work for Jeff (a friend of his that owns an auto repair shop in wichita) I worked on a fiero.  Those things are so hard to work on, and this car kept coming back all the time"  blah blah blah.  So I believed him and went on driving my firebird with all of 12 mpg, on premium, spending 70 bucks a week in gas.  so one day hes telling me a story about when his dad died and he had to quit working for Jeff, to help his mom with the business and everything.  Well I caught a slight technicallity, that blew the whole "fieros are pieces of junk" story to bits.  My grandpa died in 1976. So I pick up on this, and ask my dad again.  "Tell me why you dont like fieros?" he tells me about all the work he did on this one fiero, and how much of a piece it was, so I ask him, "aproximately what year was this?" he says ""just before your grandpa died, maybe late 1975 to early 1976, I said "dad, they didnt even start making fieros until 1984"  so he was like " I swear it was a fiero"  within 30 minutes he was changing his mind, it was something else, but then his anti fiero turns to "well if they were so great then why arent they still making them?"  I didnt have an answer, but I figured Im 21 I can do what the hell I want now, so I went to the bank got a loan and bought a fiero.  Ive put over 12,000 miles on it since late feb. and the car keeps going and going and going.  My dad doesnt have problems with fieros now, since my car is more reliable then his brand new ford van, that has something wrong with the brakes every other week, or some recall going on all the time.  I love fieros!||||reg||1
